From 06a53d3e1386251854a4fac1c5e253b97909cdee Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yihou <yihou@amd.com>
Date: Wed, 29 Jul 2026 14:29:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 02/25] sglang DSA: fix PD+MTP deadlock, add page-table row
 fix, correct idle-rank slice

Three patches for GLM-5.2 DSA on gfx950, taking PD disaggregation with
DP-attention + EAGLE MTP from "deadlocks on the first routed request" to
640/640 requests at conc=128 x 512 tokens.

dsa_indexer_hip_dp_padded_rows.diff (revised)
  The slice guard was `if 0 < q_offset < q_fp8.shape[0]`. The `0 <` lower bound
  made the slice a no-op on DP-idle ranks, where q_offset == 0 because the rank
  holds no requests -- reproducing the same "lengths.size(0) == B" assert on
  those ranks. It only surfaces once some ranks are idle while others are busy,
  which the original single-node validation never exercised. Bound removed;
  q_fp8[:0] is a legal empty slice and the CUDA path has no such bound either.

dsa_backend_dp_sync_and_page_table_rows.diff (new)
  1. Replaces `int(forward_batch.seq_lens.max().item())` with the sync-free
     `self.req_to_token.shape[1]`. That host sync sat on a branch only some DP
     ranks take, so idle peers took the cheap arm and the DP collectives
     desynchronized -- the PD+MTP deadlock. Two further unconditional .cpu()
     syncs removed. Measured: no rank reaches dsa_backend in a py-spy dump
     afterwards, and PD warmup passes on all 8 ranks.
  2. Expands page_table rows to match topk_indices rows before
     transform_index_page_table_decode. page_table_1 has one row per request,
     topk_indices one row per token; equal for plain decode, unequal under MTP,
     which killed all 8 ranks on the callee's assert. Padded topk rows are all
     -1 and masked by the kernel, so only the row count matters. Applied at both
     decode call sites.

deepseek_nextn_glm52_mtp_bf16.diff (new)
  One line. Required for GLM-5.2, whose MTP/nextn layer is bf16 while the rest
  of the model is quantized; without it the weight load dies 3072 vs 6144.

All three verified with `git apply --check` against a pristine sglang
0b3bb0cbe31873994c9f989fddfe2f87ca839fdd (v0.5.15.post1).

Measured on 2x 8xMI355X (gfx950), ROCm 7.2.0, GLM-5.2-MXFP4, mooncake RDMA over
mlx5 + dma-buf: PD warmup ~10s, 5 rounds x conc=128 x 512 tokens = 640/640
HTTP 200, 0 scheduler exceptions, 0 KVTransferError, spec-dec active with mean
accept length 2.73 across all 8 dp_ranks.

Two caveats, both outside these diffs and documented in the README:
  - measured with the EAGLE draft CUDA graph disabled. That graph's
    enable/disable decision in eagle_worker_v2.py::draft() is rank-divergent
    under DP-attention, so ranks split between graph replay and eager within one
    collective step and hang. A proper fix is not written yet, so no
    eagle_worker_v2 patch is included.
  - ~2% of responses under concurrency are degenerate (HTTP 200, right token
    count, wrong content). Root cause not established.

